UsageSummary.description:
Usage summary represents aggregated usage data for a metered [feature](/docs/api/features/feature-object) in a [subscription](/docs/api/subscriptions/subscription-object) over a specific reporting period. The aggregation is performed based on the [aggregation method](https://www.chargebee.com/docs/billing/2.0/usage-based-billing/defining-metered-features) configured in Billing.

Use this resource to analyze feature-level usage for reporting or analytics purposes, independent of usage billing or invoicing.

### Group-by attributes

When usage is grouped, each distinct set of group-by attribute values forms one group. The response returns each group as a separate `usage_summary` object with an `attributes` list containing:

* `name`: The group-by attribute name.
* `value`: The group-by attribute value for that group. A null group is returned as JSON `null`, and an empty-string group is returned as `""`.

For example:

```json
{
  "attributes": [
    {
      "name": "gpu_type",
      "value": "h100"
    },
    {
      "name": "region",
      "value": "us-east"
    }
  ]
}
```

The `attributes` list is not returned when usage is not grouped.

The order of entries in `attributes` matches the order of the names specified in `group_by`.

